                <pb facs="0676" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg594"/>

                <head>No. 4.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Maximilian, emperor of Mexico, having consulted our council of ministers, we have
                    decreed and do decree the following:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. The empire protects the Catholic
                    Apostolic and Roman religion as the religion of the state.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art.</hi> 2. All forms of worship not contrary to
                    morality, civilization, and good manners, shall have free and ample toleration
                    in all the territory of the empire. No worship can be established without the
                    previous consent of the government.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 3 As circumstances shall demand, the
                    administration, by police regulations, will arrange all that may concern the
                    exercise of worship.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 4. Abuses which may be committed by the
                    authorities against the exercise of worship, and against the liberty which the
                    laws guarantee to their ministers, shall be laid before the council of
                    state.</p>
                <p>This decree shall be placed in the archives of the empire and published in the
                    official journal.</p>
                <p>Done at the palace, at Mexico, February 26, 1865.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">MAXIMILIAN.</p>
                <p>By order of his Imperial Majesty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PEDRO ESCUDERO Y ECHANOVE, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of
                            justice.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
